---
config:
  flowchart:
    wrappingWidth: 400
---
flowchart TB
    accTitle: The title and the entry fix themselves
    accDescr: The check of the title fails. A pull request from a fork, or one with the label no-bot-fixes, stays as it is, and the PR coach explains. On a branch of the repository, the bot reads the pull request from the API. A title that names its own type and differs only in its form becomes the one that the PR coach suggests; any other stays a suggestion. When that title is a feat, fix or perf of a person with no entry of its own and no draft before, the bot commits one new file of changelog.d that it names and writes itself, and the report asks to read it. A corrected title or a draft starts the check again, which finds it fixed. What is left stays with the PR coach.

    failed(["The check of the title fails"])
    own{"A branch of the repository,<br>without no-bot-fixes?"}
    coach["What is left stays with the PR coach: it suggests<br>the title and says what the entry needs"]
    form{"The title names its own type,<br>and only its form differs?"}
    title["The bot sets the title<br>that the PR coach suggests"]
    entry{"A feat, fix or perf of a person,<br>no entry, and no draft before?"}
    draft["One new file of changelog.d that the bot<br>names and writes itself, from the title"]
    again(["The check runs again, and finds it fixed"])
    read["The report asks to read the draft"]

    failed --> own
    own -- "no" --> coach
    own -- "yes" --> form
    form -- "yes" --> title
    form -- "no" --> entry
    title --> entry
    title --> again
    entry -- "no" --> coach
    entry -- "yes" --> draft
    draft --> read
    draft --> again

    classDef bot fill:#526cfe2e,stroke:#526cfe,stroke-width:2px
    classDef person fill:#f59e0b2e,stroke:#f59e0b,stroke-width:2px
    classDef done fill:#16a34a2e,stroke:#16a34a,stroke-width:2px
    class coach,title,draft bot
    class failed,read person
    class again done
